# The CLI talks to the Daintree Assistant BACKEND, not to DeepSeek directly.
#
# DEVELOPMENT: the backend endpoint is HARDCODED to http://127.0.0.1:8473 and runs
# unauthenticated. There is intentionally no config knob for it — the assistant
# supports exactly this one endpoint for now (a later phase swaps in the production
# URL + a real login flow). Run the backend locally: it lives at ../assistant-backend
# and owns the model credentials (DEEPSEEK_API_KEY), prompt assembly, and skills.
#
# The only override is DAINTREE_BACKEND_URL, a dev/test escape hatch (e.g. pointing
# at a fake backend in e2e tests). Leave it unset in normal use.
# DAINTREE_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8473

# Daintree MCP connection (injected by Daintree when it launches the CLI).
# Leave unset to run in degraded local mode (fs/timer/watcher/queue tools only).
# DAINTREE_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:45454/mcp
# DAINTREE_MCP_TOKEN=...
# DAINTREE_PROJECT_ID=...

# Optional overrides.
# DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_TIER=system   # supervisor | operator | system
# DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_STATE_DIR=~/.daintree/assistant-cli
